{% comment %}
  A heading in two faces.

  Satoshi for the sentence, Playfair for the part being emphasised. Which part
  is the shop's decision, so it is marked in the text itself:

    Ready to scale your business with *websites and automation?*

  Nothing marked renders as an ordinary heading, so existing settings keep
  working untouched.

  Usage:
    {% render 'sm-heading', text: section.settings.heading, tag: 'h2', class: 'sm-heading sm-heading--md' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign heading_tag = tag | default: 'h2'
  assign heading_class = class | default: 'sm-heading'
  assign pieces = text | split: '*'

  comment
    Count the asterisks rather than the pieces. Liquid's `split` drops a
    trailing empty string, so a heading that ends on a closing asterisk —
    "…in *3 easy steps*" — splits into two pieces, exactly like an unclosed
    one. Counting the characters tells them apart; counting pieces does not,
    which is why the asterisks were rendering as text.
  endcomment
  assign bare = text | remove: '*' | size
  assign full = text | size
  assign marks = full | minus: bare

  assign balanced = false
  assign pairs = marks | modulo: 2
  if marks > 0 and pairs == 0
    assign balanced = true
  endif
-%}

<{{ heading_tag }} class="{{ heading_class }}">
  {%- if balanced -%}
    {%- for piece in pieces -%}
      {%- assign position = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 -%}
      {%- if position == 1 -%}
        <em class="sm-heading__accent">{{ piece }}</em>
      {%- else -%}
        {{ piece }}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {{ text }}
  {%- endif -%}
</{{ heading_tag }}>
